<title>UK: BAA down on profit-taking, press comment.</title>
<headline>BAA down on profit-taking, press comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in airport operator BAA Plc dropped on Friday, amid profit-taking after its recent sharp gains and negative press comment on its acquisition of Duty Free International, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock -- up 46-1/2p in the past two sessions to a record high -- was down 22-1/2p at 584-1/2 by 0940 GMT, in volume of 3.2 million shares.</p>
</text>
